## create combinations

Write a function, _createCombinations_, that takes in an array and a length as arguments. The
function should return a 2D array representing all of the combinations of the specifized length.

The items within the combinations and the combinations themselves may be returned in any order.

You may assume that the input array contains unique elements and 1 <= k <= items.length.

#### test_00:

```js
createCombinations(["a", "b", "c"], 2); // ->
// [
//   [ 'a', 'b' ],
//   [ 'a', 'c' ],
//   [ 'b', 'c' ]
// ]
```

#### test_01:

```js
createCombinations(["q", "r", "s", "t"], 2); // ->
// [
//   [ 'q', 'r' ],
//   [ 'q', 's' ],
//   [ 'q', 't' ],
//   [ 'r', 's' ],
//   [ 'r', 't' ],
//   [ 's', 't' ]
// ]
```

#### test_02:

```js
createCombinations(['q', 'r', 's', 't'], 3)); // ->
// [
//   [ 'q', 'r', 's' ],
//   [ 'q', 'r', 't' ],
//   [ 'q', 's', 't' ],
//   [ 'r', 's', 't' ]
// ]
```

#### test_03:

```js
createCombinations([1, 28, 94], 3); // ->
// [
//   [ 1, 28, 94 ]
// ]
```

