## solutions

#### recursive

```js
const createCombinations = (items, k) => {
  if (items.length < k) return [];

  if (k === 0) return [[]];

  const first = items[0];
  const combosWithFirst = [];
  for (let combo of createCombinations(items.slice(1), k - 1)) {
    combosWithFirst.push([first, ...combo]);
  }

  const combosWithoutFirst = createCombinations(items.slice(1), k);
  return [...combosWithFirst, ...combosWithoutFirst];
};
```

- n = length of items
- k = target length
- Time: ~O(n choose k)
- Space: ~O(n choose k)

Note: ["n Choose k"](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binomial_coefficient) refers to the binomial coefficient.

