## solutions

#### recursive

```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <string>

std::vector<std::vector<std::string>> createCombinations(std::vector<std::string> items, int size) {
  if (size == 0) {
    return std::vector<std::vector<std::string>> { {} };
  }

  if (size > items.size()) {
    return std::vector<std::vector<std::string>> { };
  }

  std::string el = items[0];
  std::vector<std::string> remaining = std::vector<std::string>(items.begin() + 1, items.end());

  std::vector<std::vector<std::string>> result;

  for (std::vector<std::string> comb : createCombinations(remaining, size)) {
    result.push_back(comb);
  }

  for (std::vector<std::string> comb : createCombinations(remaining, size - 1)) {
    comb.push_back(el);
    result.push_back(comb);
  }

  return result;
}
```

- n = size of items
- k = target size
- Time: ~O(n choose k)
- Space: ~O(n choose k)

Note: ["n Choose k"](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binomial_coefficient) refers to the binomial coefficient.
